                        

Item #:  SCP-5232 

Object Class:  Safe

Threat Level:  Blue

Special Containment Procedures:  [All information regarding SCP-5170 is to be hidden from level 1 personnel or less, if a person of such level accesses information regarding SCP-5170 they are to be immediately terminated. SCP-5232 is to be kept in a 30m2 cell and protocol 202-5232-A

Protocol 202-5232-A forbids any foundation personnel to enter the cell unless they have already come within 30m of this SCP before the protocol was in place, tests with D-CLASS on SCP-5232 is still allowed as long as as the test is done by a level 3 or higher researcher.

Any cleaning of SCP-5232's cell is to be done by a D-CLASS janitor or any janitor who has come in contact with SCP-5232 beforehand and survived.

It has also been concluded impossible to destroy SCP-5232 and impossible to stop it rolling.

Description:  [SCP-5232 is a six-sided black dice, with the classic dots on each side showing the number value of the side (these dots are white). SCP-5232 does not show any anomalies properties until an alive entity (human, animal, plant and SCP all included) comes within 30m2 of the SCP, if an alive entity comes within 30m2 -which researchers call SCP-5232's judgment zone- the dice will then proceed to roll itself appearing to be a completely random roll.

Once it has done this, if the top of the dice shows a 1-5 then the entity is safe however if the top of the dice shows a six then the entity shall die and have nothing they can do about it (the form of death is recorded as infinite and again this appears to be selected as random and not by the SCP its-self

Researches Nicknamed SCP-5232 sixes because of its death on a roll of six anomalous properties.]








CLASS-D:  [D-4546B]

Researcher:  [Nadiva Raghe]

Foreword:  [Test shows two examples of unsuccessfully stopping SCP-5232's anomalous propities]

 

Researcher:  [D-4546B please enter the cell and proceed to clamp the dice with the equipment you were given]

CLASS-D:  [O Kwhat should I observe for?]

Researcher:  [Anything out of the ordinary, NO more questions!]

Researcher:  [Interesting. The dice appears to be melting the clamps and continue to roll itself]

CLASS-D:  [I..Is that bad? It looks like its stopped.]

Researcher:  [D-4546B I cannot see the number on the top of the dice, what does it show?]

CLASS-D:  [It shows a six, why?]

Researcher:  [Hmmm, ok I have an idea. D-4546B please proceed to leave the room. You have finished the test]

CLASS-D:  [Ohthank you Dr I hope I did we-]

CLASS-D:  [*AHHHHHHHHHhhh* *silence*]

Researcher:  [Ok so it appears by leaves the area death still happens. Cause of death: Acid burning, this is a new one.]

Researcher 2:  [So Dr Nadiva how did the test go and what did we find out?]

Researcher:  [Nothing especially exciting, the subject still died despite leaving the room.]

Researcher 2:  [Ok I shall bring in another D-CLASS, this time I want to see if the subject can be hidden from view and the dice will still roll. Oh that reminds me I'm guessing the idea of clamping the dice in one place didn't work?]

Researcher:  [That is correct.]

Researcher 2:  [Ok, prepare to start a new log.]

 

Closing Statement:  [Next test shows ████████]








                    

                                    





            
    

                    



                    
                        
                            
